# N2 (the author, 2026-10-18, LMX_blog/2026-10-18.md; Codex FABLE-REVIEW-PATH-UNIFY-20261018T1635Z on 9e1a40d0): the effect of a
# path is its resolved record's -- the root it starts at and the reference fields it crosses -- never the name of a segment.
# A\mid\v crosses no reference: A's mid is an inline nested Structure.  B, unrelated, has a reference field of the same name
# mid.  read follows no nullable reference, so its native signature has no status channel (Debt pins the exact signature; the
# old name heuristic, matching `mid` against every reference field of the unit, put the channel on).  Entry 7.
Model: (int: v 7)
A:
    mid:
        int: v 7
    end: mid
end: A
B:
    @: mid Model
    int: k 1
end: B
fn: read () int
    return: A\mid\v
end: read
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: read(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
